WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.900
Takato and the gang knew they had to go to the digital world to save Kalamon.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.980
The problem was finding a way in.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.040
But Gilman eventually dug one up.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.920
But to believe it was right under his house?

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.260
Now all they had to do was tell their families.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.780
Henry told Susie about Terryman being real,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.940
and she acted like she'd known it all along.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.280
Rika's grandma finally met Renamon and gave them the thumbs up.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.700
Takato's mom didn't take it quite so well.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.820
But his dad knew Takato was in good hands.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.160
Even Yamaki had a little going-away present.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.630
Looks like they're all set.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:29.970
I just hope they know what they're doing.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.300
What are you doing?

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:35.050
Well, ladies and gentlemen, we're officially the pioneers of the digital world.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.730
Oh, please, just stay focused. We're here to find Kelamon.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.970
And be careful. The laws of the real world may not apply here.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.350
You're telling me I almost got hit in the mouth with a floating question mark.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:51.770
All right, I... here. Hold on, okay?

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.220
Thank you, Rika. Much better.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.040
All right, guys, let's go.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:56.600
Yeah!

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.140
Where are we, anyway?

00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.980
A data field, an ocean of...

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:07.720
I want to let go, Takato. I think I'm going to be sick.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.180
I'm right behind you, dude.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.280
It must have been a data search. Maybe new information changes spatial relationships.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.700
I'll have to change something, too. This keeps up.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.780
But which way is up and which way is down?

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.860
It's all the same. Up or down depends on you.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.820
Well, that makes a whole lot of sense.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.950
I think that way is down.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.200
Oh, dear.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.390
There's another bread!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:21.140
I've dirt. Huh?

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.900
Yeoman, are you okay?

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.510
It's gone. The bread went bye-bye.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.970
Is that earth?

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:33.670
Wait a minute. Did we fall from all the way up there?

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:35.880
That's right, Brad.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.300
There's just no way.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.410
It's so far away.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.180
Can't believe we weren't hurt.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:44.890
Rika, are you all right?

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.760
All things considered, yeah, I'm fine.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.760
Welcome to the digital world, ladies.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.320
Do you need a hand?

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.600
We've got to find a new way of getting here.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.500
So this is the digital world.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.970
Did you expect everything to look like a...

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:06.930
No, I guess I pictured something different. I just never thought it would be so real

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:18.920
Hey, what's that? I don't know it looks like a movie from here

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:29.780
Beautiful those themes are gigantic and they lead right up to the real world. They're everywhere. What?

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:33.690
they do you think they must be streams of data being transferred between our

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.890
world in this one anytime you use a computer I bet it sends one of those

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:42.920
beams to extract the information from down here we go that's one small step

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:48.380
Vermont one giant leap for mankind bad this place is humongous can we go search

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.780
for the bread now you never give up do you we came here to find Calamon enough

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:59.980
with the bread hey over here we're the first humans to step foot

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.130
digital world. Picture time. Now let's get busy.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:04.720
Smiles, everyone.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.760
Liomon, forget it.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.000
Oh, terrific. Another camera test.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.500
Let's make sure to get our flag in the shot.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.960
Okay, everyone get in tighter.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.380
Remember, the camera is your friend.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.680
Liomon, could you... thank you.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.170
Nice! Ooh, very nice.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.840
Okay, group shot. Everyone try to be natural.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:29.630
Oh, nuts!

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.060
Now that Kenta's little fashion shoot's over,

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:35.740
shouldn't we start looking for Calamon?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.480
Rika's right. Who knows? Maybe this can help.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.600
What's that? Some kind of fruit finder?

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.380
No, Yamaki said it was a comm device.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:46.000
What? System error? That's weird.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:46.800
I'll reboot.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.880
Hmm. The data streams must be messing with the signal.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:51.520
I'm not getting anything.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.920
Oh, man. Huh?

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.700
What gives? Something's wrong with my camera.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:56.480
Let me see it.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.970
That's weird. They're pixelated.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.500
They're pix-a-what-it?

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.280
Fuzzy, Penta. They're fuzzy.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:05.660
Ful-tized. Bad.

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.880
I don't get it. It worked fine when we were back in the real world.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:09.260
Mm-hmm.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:10.120
Hey, guys!

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:10.870
Huh?

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.140
This thing's fried, too. It won't connect.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:16.270
Hmm.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:17.670
I wonder.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.690
Those data streams must be interfering with anything that's digital.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.780
As long as we're anywhere near them,

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.760
the electronics we brought with us will probably be useless.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.980
So basically, you're saying that we're...

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.410
Brilliant deduction, Sherlock.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.570
Um, we gonna get home.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:36.450
Huh?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.610
If we can't communicate, how are we supposed to find our way back?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.870
I don't want to be stuck here forever.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:46.070
Who's gonna feed this school? I mean, my hamster.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:48.010
We lost a lot of supplies in the fall,

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:50.550
and I don't see any convenience stores anywhere in this desert.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.590
Man, a mega slushy sounds good right now.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.730
Come on, you guys, you sound like you're giving up before even trying.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:59.090
Look, the Digimon all traveled to the real world from here somehow,

00:06:59.290 --> 00:06:59.970
so we just have to...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.950
find that portal, okay? If there's a way in, there's gotta be a way out, right?

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:10.720
Exactly. Good point, Takato. See? Now that's what I'm talking about. Come on,

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:18.540
didn't we all come here to rescue Kalamon? Huh? Yeah! Right, then let's go find the

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:24.750
little guy. Momentime. Yeah, but where do we even begin? Where are we, anyway? Well,

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:29.840
see, that's a problem. Buckleheads! Huh? There's something on the horizon!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.270
Maybe a bunch of antennae.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.040
That's a long ways away.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:39.270
Are you sure? She's right.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.310
That does look like an antenna. That means

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.200
there might be a city. I wonder if they have

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.380
digital chili dogs. Mega slushies,

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.550
here we come. Well, yep.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:50.900
I see it. Let's move. Do you think

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:54.690
Calamon? Well, we'll find out.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:56.930
If not, I'm sure there's someone there

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:57.910
that can help us find him.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.340
I think my feet fell off.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.450
Suck it up, boys.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:46.270
According to Henry's calculations, we should be there any second.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:47.090
We better be.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:50.010
I have enough sand in my shoes to start my own private beach.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:52.370
At least you've only got it in your shoes.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.670
I'm finished.

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:56.050
Good idea.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.450
Let's take a break.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:00.820
Rocks look familiar?

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:01.570
Huh?

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.290
They look a lot like antenna.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.570
Oh, no, don't you guys get it?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.690
This is the city.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:08.930
It's just a bunch of rocks.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.070
It was a mirage.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:11.190
It can't be.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.630
I could swear it was an antenna.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:14.350
We all thought so, too, Rika.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.870
Yeah, but we wasted so much time because of me.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:17.710
I hate that.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:18.710
It was an easy mistake.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:19.750
Don't blame yourself.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:20.490
Wow.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.130
Did somebody make these things?

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:25.710
It appears to be natural, but it's just fragments of human-made data.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.310
So what are we supposed to do now?

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:28.350
I have an idea.

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:29.290
Let's eat.

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:29.770
Yeah!

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:33.290
But, Tocato, we have no food. We lost it in the fall, remember?

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:34.730
Oh, I forgot.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.490
No sweat. You can have my gummy fleas.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.660
And I'd be happy to share my cookies.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.160
I mean, we are a team, aren't we?

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.940
I don't know about the fleas, but I'd love a cookie.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.030
What's that?

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.950
It's just a packet of old data.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.470
Um, guys, it's coming right at us.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:56.670
Maybe they want some cookies, too?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.750
There's nowhere to go.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:07.320
I just hold it right there, you two.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.100
Would you stop running?

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.660
It's just old data, completely harmless.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.200
They must be sensing something.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.870
Huh? Are you sure?

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:17.790
I don't see anything.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.920
Look, down by the end of the rock towers.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:21.880
It's coming.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.830
It's turning dark.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.210
Is this normal?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:30.760
I hope so!

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.090
Nobody panic.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:36.070
What just happened?

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.440
Oh, it turned off the color!

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.680
Is it nighttime now?

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:41.540
How weird.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.900
No dusk, just darkness.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.100
That was the fastest sunset I've ever seen!

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:46.360
More like a switch.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.600
I guess that's how it works here.

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:49.560
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.320
Data streams hitting pretty close to us.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.300
If that hit us, what would happen?

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:59.840
Those streams pull massive amounts of information.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:07.200
From the surface of this world and transfer it to wherever the user specifies if it did hit us who knows where we might end up

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:14.470
Rika, what is it? We have company where I don't see anything

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:15.710
Right

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.970
And from the looks of it, he's not too happy

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.660
Be on guard, everyone. Let's see what he's up to.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:38.020
Meromon, champion level. His special attack is Magma Blast.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:38.680
Great.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:40.640
Yeah, I wonder what he wants.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:42.620
Magma Blast!

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:02.710
Are you ready?

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:03.290
Yes.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:05.410
That's enough!

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.130
Fist of the Beast King!

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:19.400
Are you okay?

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:20.430
Mm-mm.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:25.200
You're happy!

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:27.340
You evil fiends have finally defeated me!

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.680
Go ahead, absorb my data!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.960
I'm ready for you.

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:32.940
We wouldn't have hurt you if you hadn't attacked.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.140
Did the devas send you?

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:35.420
Devas?

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.120
Hey, wait.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.580
You're not a Digimon.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:39.080
Huh?

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:40.920
Well, no, I'm a human being.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:42.080
What?

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:42.720
Human?

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:44.280
Are you from the real world?

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:44.660
Yeah.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:47.380
We came here to rescue a friend, and then you attacked us.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:48.280
I beg your pardon.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.180
I thought you were those monstrous creatures.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:51.400
I'm so sorry.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.270
Hey, Marimon, maybe you can help us.

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:55.030
Okay, this is our friend Calamon.

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:57.970
He was kidnapped by this creature, Makurimon.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.750
So, have you seen them?

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:04.640
Let me see. I'm very well traveled throughout this part of the world, so there's always a chance.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.660
Hey, Kenta, don't you think Maramon would make a great partner for me?

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.280
I was thinking for me.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:14.730
I'm sorry, but I don't remember seeing them.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:15.440
No dice?

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:21.830
No, I'm afraid not. You know, I thought traveling to the real world was only a myth.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:26.990
Now I long for the day when I become powerful enough to go there on my own.

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:29.960
Every night I...

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:34.040
It's so close, so beautiful.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.440
Yeah, it sure is.

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.680
I wonder when we'll see it again.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:52.080
Bob, I was just kidding!

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:59.440
A shooting star.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:07.440
This place never ceases to amaze me, yet all Miramon dreams of is fighting and getting strong enough to go to the real world.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:08.580
I wonder why.

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:10.350
He just can't help it.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:11.900
Hey, couldn't sleep either?

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:15.540
No way, not a wink. Too wired. How about you?

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:18.370
Same thing. Hey, why did you say he can't help it?

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:22.690
Well, he's like all Digimon. I think they just don't know any other way to live.

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:28.160
And until they met us, Terriamon, Renamon, and Leamon were the same way.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:29.890
Yeah, but that's so sad.

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:32.420
Guillemon never...

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:32.740
Oh.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:35.160
Huh?

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:36.360
What's up?

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:37.410
Hmm.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:40.500
What's the matter?

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:42.040
I hear something.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:43.620
What is it, Renemon?

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.870
What's that sound?

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:46.930
I don't know.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:50.900
Harry, wake up.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:52.000
Hear that?

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:53.010
Hear what?

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:57.400
Jagamon.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.960
Ultimate level plant Digimon that travel in her...

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:04.910
I don't know. It doesn't say.

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.020
Oh, great.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:09.760
It's like they're turning.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:11.850
They're coming right at us.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.390
Let's move, heads.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.700
Don't you stand there, run for it.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:21.860
Huh?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.080
It's the law of the digital world.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:02.960
Fine.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:06.800
Things here can be cruel sometimes to go.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:11.320
What are you flying?

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:12.050
Fishy?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:17.360
Learn how to do that?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.480
Will you teach me?

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:19.440
Please?

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:32.610
Oh, did I sleep good?

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.280
Huh? They're up early.

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:38.020
Maybe they're giving Rika some personality lessons.

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:41.220
Kenta, wake up. Quit being a lazy blob, dude.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.510
Huh? Hey, who took my blue blackie?

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:46.950
Grow up.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:49.060
Huh?

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:50.820
Breakfast, anyone?

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.500
Goodbye, Aramon.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.240
Your fire burned bright, my friend.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:57.750
We can't eat this!

00:16:58.110 --> 00:16:58.230
Huh?

00:16:58.930 --> 00:16:59.970
Hold him, Kenta!

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.540
I am holding him.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:04.220
Guess who's awake?

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:05.160
Oh, no.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.120
Please, you can't go with my tail.

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.740
I'll do anything you want, I promise.

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:12.790
Jagamon, you're in a lot of trouble for what you did last night.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:13.690
What do you mean?

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:16.950
He and his friends caused a stampede that almost flattened us.

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:17.490
Yeah.

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:20.480
Merrimon didn't make it.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:21.220
Hmm?

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:22.700
Explain yourself.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.530
We only wanted to protect ourselves.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:26.750
You hurt him.

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:29.670
I think Merrimon was trying to take over their territory.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.970
I'm shocked.

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:33.680
He's sorry, see?

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.760
Well, that just isn't good enough, see?

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:36.700
Stop it, Rika.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.880
Takato, show Jagamon the pictures of Kalamon and Makuramon.

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:41.560
Maybe he's seen them in the area.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:43.720
Hi, have you seen him?

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.490
It's okay, we're not gonna hurt you.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.420
He's a little guy.

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:52.110
Okay, uh, how about this one?

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.150
Oh, how you doing? Did all of you see him? Can you tell us when?

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.780
Oh, oh, oh, okay. How about where?

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.160
Do you think we can believe them?

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:15.090
Don't you think it's strange that they saw Makuromon but not Kalomon?

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:19.760
Listen up. Are you lying to us about seeing that monkey?

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:21.980
Lying? What is lying?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:26.590
My turn. Now you remember seeing Makuromon, right?

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.170
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:29.620
Good. Okay.

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:30.330
Where?

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:35.890
Hey, which way did he go?

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:37.080
That way!

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.480
Open the door!

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:11.180
We've been dropped, lost, starved, attacked, and stampeded.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:16.220
Yeah, if we were back home, I'd be in social studies right now, catching up on my sleep.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:18.200
It's only going to get more intense.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.360
We haven't even faced Makoramon yet.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:21.540
We'll be ready for him.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.660
And we'll get Kalamon back, too.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:24.840
Yeah, but at what price?

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.380
You saw what happened to Miramon.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:27.720
This place can be brutal.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:29.980
Gilmon, I want you to...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:34.880
you to be really, really careful while we're here, okay? No funny stuff. You gotta promise

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:40.080
me something, that nothing bad will happen. Nothing bad's going to happen. Don't worry.

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:48.180
But promise me. I promise. Now, what about that bread? Huh? Guys, look out! What now? Behind

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:57.240
you! Huh? It's a data stream. That's not good? Not good at all. Shouldn't we be running

00:19:57.240 --> 00:19:58.940
by now? Yeah, let's go.

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:14.530
Right!

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:32.680
This doesn't look good at all.

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:35.660
Can the guys be blown to the other side of the digital world?

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.860
Find out on the next Digimon Digital Monsters.
